<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fustat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fustat was the first Arab capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amr-ibn-al-as">Amr ibn al-As</a> around 641 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>'s conquest. It became a major commercial city, and it remained an important centre after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> nearby. It was later absorbed into Cairo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fustat.jpg" alt="Fustat" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rappoport, A.S. (Angelo Solomon), 1871-1950 VIAF (71482297) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fostat-329.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
